<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  BugTurretRetexture_GeonosianHive.xml       Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-29
  ============================================================================

  Owner, 2026-08-29 (verbatim): "Gotta redo the art on those cartoonish bug
  turrets." VFEI2_Vilelobber, VFEI2_Thornworm and VFEI2_Thornspitter are all
  ruled into the Geonosian Foundry Hive faction's art register
  (design/Jawa/art/FACTION_ART_SPEC.md ~line 297: "chitinous, brutal,
  trophy-laden ... a hive mouth or a caste mark. Rust.") - the donor mod's flat
  cel-shaded blob-with-nub-limbs art reads as too cartoonish for that register.

  ⚠️ VFEI2_Vilelobber and VFEI2_Thornworm SHARED ONE texPath in the donor mod
  (Things/Building/InsectoidTurrets/InsectoidTurret_Base) despite being
  different creatures with different stats/projectiles - they rendered
  IDENTICAL in game. Each now gets its OWN unique file; the collision is gone,
  not just recoloured.

  New art, one per defName, painted to the Geonosian Foundry Hive brief:
  rusted iron plate fused with chitin, riveted bone/skull trophies at the rim,
  a dark hive-mouth aperture at centre. Differentiated per the owner's brief
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/faction_equipment_clusters.md,
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/Alien_Bestiary.md - fabrication-hive, not
  nature-hive):
    Vilelobber   (2x2) - acid sacs and corrosive yellow-green ichor dripping
                         from the maw (it spits acid).
    Thornworm    (2x2) - a crown of bone-white chitin thorn spikes around a
                         dark segmented worm-ring maw (it ejects thorns), no
                         acid - the visual differentiator from Vilelobber.
    Thornspitter (1x1) - the same thorn family, deliberately smaller and
                         cruder: one rusted collar ring, four thorns, no
                         trophies - reads as the small/tiny sibling mound.

  Canvas kept at the donor's own size (256x256 / 256x256 / 128x128 =
  128px-per-cell-occupancy for 2x2/2x2/1x1, per the generating-rimworld-sprites
  skill's ruling) - no upscale needed, the donor was already at-spec.
  graphicClass on all three is Verse.Graphic_Single (confirmed against the
  2026-08-29T20-07-29Z def dump) - one texture per def, no facing suffixes.

  🔴 CORRECTED 2026-08-30, live load harvest (harvest_log.py): the original
  version of this file used PatchOperationReplace on
  Defs/ThingDef[defName="..."]/graphicData/texPath for all three defs, and
  Vilelobber and Thornworm FAILED AT ACTUAL LOAD -
  "[Jawa Patches (local)] Patch operation Verse.PatchOperationFindMod(Vanilla
  Factions Expanded - Insectoids 2) failed" - even though validate_patch.py
  against the live def dump reported 0 errors. The dump reflects the
  POST-inheritance C# object, which is why the xpath looked fine offline; the
  real mechanism is the opposite of what was assumed:
  `skills/rimworld-modding/references/patch-operations.md` §5 -
  "Inheritance is resolved AFTER patches run. Patches operate on the literal
  [XML as written on disk]." Read on THIS disk: Vilelobber and Thornworm each
  declare `<ThingDef ParentName="VFEI2_TurretBase">` with NO literal
  `<graphicData>` node of their own at all - it is 100% inherited from the
  abstract parent (Buildings_Insectoid.xml:2397). A Replace on a node that does
  not exist in the raw tree matches zero and the operation fails (it is NOT the
  "matches nothing logs nothing" PatchOperationConditional case - Replace
  wrapped only in FindMod/Sequence has no such grace). Thornspitter is
  different: it DOES declare its own literal `<graphicData>` (a different
  texPath, different drawSize) - its Replace op below was never broken and is
  unchanged.

  THE FIX for Vilelobber/Thornworm: PatchOperationAdd, not Replace, inserting a
  whole new `<graphicData>` element as a direct child of each ThingDef -
  replicating every field VFEI2_TurretBase's graphicData declares (drawSize
  1.5x1.5, drawOffset, damageData/rect, shadowData) except texPath, which
  points at the new Jawa art. Read straight off VFEI2_TurretBase's own XML
  (Buildings_Insectoid.xml:2400-2412), not guessed - dropping any of those
  fields would silently revert to a C# default the moment the child's own
  literal graphicData node exists (object-typed fields REPLACE on inheritance,
  they do not merge field-by-field; only LIST-typed fields append).

  Scope: ART ONLY. Damage, projectiles and the "sonic re-projectile" idea on
  Vilelobber's turret_register.json row are untouched - that is a separate,
  still-open (contested: true) mechanical decision, not this patch's job.

  ⛔ DO NOT EDIT THE WORKSHOP FOLDER. Steam overwrites it on the next update.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Vanilla Factions Expanded - Insectoids 2</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- Vilelobber has NO literal graphicData of its own (100% inherited
             from VFEI2_TurretBase) - ADD the whole node, not Replace one field
             of it. Every field but texPath copied verbatim from the base. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEI2_Vilelobber"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <graphicData>
              <texPath>Things/Building/InsectoidTurrets/Jawa_Vilelobber_Base</texPath>
              <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
              <drawSize>(1.5, 1.5)</drawSize>
              <drawOffset>(0,0,-0.1)</drawOffset>
              <damageData>
                <rect>(0.2,0.2,0.6,0.6)</rect>
              </damageData>
              <shadowData>
                <volume>(1.5,0.35,1.4)</volume>
                <offset>(0,0,-0.05)</offset>
              </shadowData>
            </graphicData>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Thornworm: same situation as Vilelobber, same base, same fix. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEI2_Thornworm"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <graphicData>
              <texPath>Things/Building/InsectoidTurrets/Jawa_Thornworm_Base</texPath>
              <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
              <drawSize>(1.5, 1.5)</drawSize>
              <drawOffset>(0,0,-0.1)</drawOffset>
              <damageData>
                <rect>(0.2,0.2,0.6,0.6)</rect>
              </damageData>
              <shadowData>
                <volume>(1.5,0.35,1.4)</volume>
                <offset>(0,0,-0.05)</offset>
              </shadowData>
            </graphicData>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Thornspitter DOES declare its own literal graphicData/texPath
             (Buildings_Insectoid.xml:2656-2668, its own drawSize/shadowData,
             not the shared base's) - this Replace was never broken, unchanged. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEI2_Thornspitter"]/graphicData/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>Things/Building/InsectoidTurrets/Jawa_ThornspitterSmall_Base</texPath></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
